def find_fixed_point(arr):
    left, right = 0, len(arr) - 1

    while left < right:
        mid = (left + right) // 2

        if arr[mid] > arr[mid + 1]:
            return mid
        elif arr[mid] < arr[mid - 1]:
            return mid - 1
        else:
            # Check for potential fixed point
            if arr[left] <= arr[mid]:
                right = mid
            else:
                left = mid + 1

    return -1
```

The provided solution uses binary search to efficiently find the fixed point in linear time complexity O(log n). The check function verifies the correctness of the generated function using the provided test cases.

