def min_sum_path(triangle):
    # Start from the second last row of the triangle
    for i in range(len(triangle) - 2, -1, -1):
        for j in range(i + 1):
            # Update the current element by adding the minimum of its left and right values
            triangle[i][j] += min(triangle[i+1][j], triangle[i+1][j+1])

    return triangle[0][0]
```

This solution iterates through each row of the triangle, starting from the second-to-last row (since we want to consider all elements up to the first element). For each cell, it updates the value by taking the minimum of the two adjacent cells from the previous row. This approach ensures that we always have access to the smallest possible sums at each step, leading to the minimum total path sum.

