def max_sum_subseq(arr):
    n = len(arr)
    dp = [0] * (n + 1)

    for i in range(1, n + 1):
        for j in range(i - 1, -1, -1):
            if arr[j] < arr[i - 1]:
                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] + arr[i])

    return dp[n]
```

The provided solution uses dynamic programming to solve the problem. It initializes a list `dp` where `dp[i]` represents the maximum sum of subsequence ending at index `i`. For each element in the input array, it iterates backward from the end of the array to the beginning, updating the `dp` values accordingly. The final result is stored in `dp[n]`, which gives the maximum sum of any subsequence of the original array that does not contain adjacent elements.

