The `maximum_segments` function calculates the maximum number of segments that can be formed by dividing the total number of elements `n`, divided by the numbers of elements `a`, `b`, and `c`. This approach works because each segment starts at an element divisible by `a`, ends at an element divisible by `b`, and includes an element divisible by `c` before it. By multiplying these three values and taking their ceiling, we ensure that all segments will contain one element from each group of sizes `a`, `b`, and `c`.

